#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Gathers the local sample set for PLAN.md step 0.8 and writes samples/manifest.json.

Copies test fixtures from ace3's checkout into samples/ace3/, which is in git, makes the
end-to-end test's email in samples/ace4/, which is too, and makes benign samples that ace3's repository doesn't hold as files into samples/local/, which
.gitignore keeps out of git. The local ones follow the fixtures ace3's tests build in
code, so both systems see the same shapes.

Every sample records where it came from, its sha256, the kinds of file it covers, and the
unit it is scanned as: its path inside an alert and the yara_meta tags it would carry.
An email is the alert's root file, named email.rfc822 the way the journal collector names
it, with no tags. Anything else arrives as an email attachment: ace3 names an attachment
after itself at the alert's top level and tags it type=email.attachment
(ace3/saq/modules/email/rfc822.py).

Usage: tools/samples/gather [--ace3 PATH]
PATH defaults to ../ace3 beside this checkout. Needs 7z on PATH for the encrypted archives.
Encrypted archives get a random salt, so their sha256 changes on every run; rerun this
script rather than editing the manifest by hand.
"""

